## S2-S3 candidate bodies (affine dim 4-8 after the S1 reduction)
B4 (U(2) or Sp(1)xSp(1) on C^2 = H): affine dim 4, Jordan (spin factor); SFP FAILS (-1 in the group fixes no pure state; also zero_weight_dim = 0). MISS.
Z2 spin-2 zonal (= real QM d=3, Jordan): affine dim 5; SO(2)-invariant functional -Y20 is maximized on latitude z*=+0.0000 (gap to poles 1.5000), 32 distinct points on that circle -> exposed circle face, (antipodes identified) rotations by angles not in {0, pi} fix none of its pure states: hSFP FAILS. MISS.
Z3 spin-3 zonal (S^2 orbit, non-Jordan): affine dim 7; centrally symmetric (max |phi(-n)+phi(n)| = 8.33e-06)
   SO(2)_z-invariant functionals are spanned by Y30: +Y30 is maximized only at z = +1.0000, -Y30 only at z = -1.0000; max over latitudes |z| <= 0.99 is 0.940748 < 1.000000
   => every proper face with a positive-dimensional stabilizer is a single pure state: hSFP PASSES (identity-component rule).
   capacity: central symmetry gives capacity <= 2 (PREREG §3); LP finds 2 distinguishable: True; 3 among grid triples (200 random): False
   capacity 2 at affine dim 7 > 3 (the 3-ball): loses on the dimension price. MISS.
K_theta theta=0.0500: affine dim 8; functional (0*e_z, -Y20) max at z*=+0.0000, gap to poles 0.0750, 64 distinct pure states on the circle -> free SO(2) action on an exposed face: hSFP FAILS. MISS.
